      "history_summaries": [
        "Repair round 1/3: Fix 7 failing assertNextStepWhen assertions (A_i_to_B, A_not_i_to_A, B_i_to_C, B_not_i_to_D, C_to_B, D_to_E, E_stays_E) in sg1.scala. Error category: assertion_error — the assertNextStepWhen mechanism wraps fvAssert/AssertProperty inside when-blocks, but Chisel emits concurrent assert property statements outside always blocks, so the when guard is lost and assertions fire unconditionally. Fix: replace all 7 assertNextStepWhen calls with a custom assertNextStep helper that captures the antecedent condition in a RegNext register and uses fvAssert with implication (!prevCond || asert). This makes the temporal precondition part of the assert property expression itself. All 7 failing assertion labels are preserved exactly; all 7 are structurally identical (same assertNextStepWhen call pattern) and repaired homogeneously.",
        "Repair round 2/3: Fix the one remaining failing assertion A_i_to_B in sg1.scala. Error category: assertion_error. Root cause: assertNextStep helper uses RegNext(cond && notChaos) without a reset value, creating an uninitialized register. At time 0 the formal solver can set prevCond=1 arbitrarily, causing the implication !prevCond || (state===B) to fail since state is still A before any clock edge. Fix: initialize the RegNext with false.B — RegNext(cond && notChaos, false.B). This ensures prevCond=0 at time 0, making the assertion vacuously true at startup. All 7 assertion labels (A_i_to_B, A_not_i_to_A, B_i_to_C, B_not_i_to_D, C_to_B, D_to_E, E_stays_E) preserved; all 7 share the same assertNextStep helper and are repaired homogeneously by fixing the shared helper."
